# Upstream CVEs — only vulnerabilities that have NO upstream fix AND are not
# reachable/applicable in the temporal-server rock are ignored here. Anything
# with a fixed version is resolved by bumping the Go toolchain / module deps in
# the rockcraft.yaml build parts and must NOT be added here.

# CVE pending review: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-crqm-pwhx-j97f
CVE-2024-34156

# --- No-fix OS / tooling CVEs (temporal-server 1.24-1.31 scans) ---

# shadow-utils (login.defs) - subuid/subgid collision only affects multi-user hosts;
# the rock runs a single service user in a container. Not reachable.
CVE-2024-56433
# glibc (libc-bin) - overflow requires an attacker-controlled fopen() mode string;
# temporal-server never passes untrusted input as a mode string. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-18374
# tar - TOCTOU / hardlink escape only triggers when extracting attacker-crafted
# archives; temporal-server does not run tar on untrusted input. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-18477
CVE-2026-18508
# systemd (libsystemd0) - journald terminal-output flaw; the rock logs via pebble,
# not journald, and ships no interactive user terminals. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-40228
# zlib1g - heap overflow in a rarely-used zlib path; Ubuntu fix deferred and
# temporal-server does not exercise the affected API. Not practically exploitable.
CVE-2026-85091
# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp - unmaintained OpenPGP package; temporal-server does
# not import or use x/crypto/openpgp. Not reachable.
GO-2026-5932

# rust-coreutils (uutils) - local TOCTOU / logic flaws in coreutils utilities that
# require local shell access; the rock ships no interactive shell and runs a single
# service user. Not reachable in this workload. No fixed version published yet.
CVE-2026-35341
CVE-2026-35344
CVE-2026-35345
CVE-2026-35348
CVE-2026-35350
CVE-2026-35351
